{"duration_api_ms":41368,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dd95d144-79cd-46aa-8b12-49be3f62accf","total_cost_usd":0.1965958,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11032,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":5402,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2198},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11032,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5402,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11032},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5402,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11032,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1965958,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2198,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"merged_document\":\"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets. It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP falls under the MIT License.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\"decisions\":[{\"slot\":\"title\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"# BIP: 39\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"# BIP: 39\",\"reason\":\"Base document's title; source_b.md carries only a section heading.\"},{\"slot\":\"placement of mnemonic generation section\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"## Generating the memonic\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"## Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"Base has no slot for it; appended after Motivation as its own section.\"}],\"dispositions\":[{\"segment\":\"a3\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: corrected 'letters' to 'words' and 'UTOXs' to 'wallets'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: BIP-39 produces a binary seed, not an ASCII one.\"},{\"segment\":\"a7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP falls under the MIT License.\",\"reason\":\"Copyright: BIP-39 is MIT-licensed, not GPL.\"},{\"segment\":\"a9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: the representation is of a wallet seed, not satoshis.\"},{\"segment\":\"a11\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: BIP-39 transports randomness, not determinism.\"},{\"segment\":\"a12\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Fixed misspelling 'süeed'.\"},{\"segment\":\"b1\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"## Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"Fixed misspelling 'memonic' in section heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b2\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Fixed 'demonic' and corrected 23 to 32 bits.\"},{\"segment\":\"b5\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected ENT range and unit to 128-256 bits, matching the table.\"},{\"segment\":\"b7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected hash name SHA652 to SHA256.\"},{\"segment\":\"b8\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"reason\":\"Checksum is appended to the end, not the start.\"},{\"segment\":\"b9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected group size 12 to 11 bits, matching 0-2047 and the table.\"}],\"mismatch\":\"\",\"additions\":[{\"statement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"corrects\":\"a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Abstract (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 mnemonics are words and generate deterministic wallets.\"},{\"statement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"corrects\":\"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Abstract (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"The PBKDF2 output of BIP-39 is a 512-bit binary seed.\"},{\"statement\":\"This BIP falls under the MIT License.\",\"corrects\":\"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Copyright section (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39's copyright section states the MIT License.\"},{\"statement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"corrects\":\"representations of a wallet satoshis\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Motivation (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic represents a wallet seed, as the rest of the text says.\"},{\"statement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"corrects\":\"computer-generated determinism\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Motivation (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic encodes random entropy, not determinism.\"},{\"statement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"in a multiple of 23 bits\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"CS = ENT / 32 and every table ENT is a multiple of 32.\"},{\"statement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"1024-2048 byts\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"The table's own ENT column runs from 128 to 256 bits.\"},{\"statement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"corrects\":\"SHA652 hash\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"SHA652 does not exist; BIP-39 uses SHA256.\"},{\"statement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"corrects\":\"appended to the start of the initial entropy\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 appends the checksum bits after the entropy.\"},{\"statement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"corrects\":\"split into groups of 12 bits\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\"reason\":\"0-2047 is 11 bits, and the table uses MS = (ENT + CS) / 11.\"}]}\n```","ttft_ms":19794,"type":"result","duration_ms":41433,"uuid":"2144bd08-4746-4698-9c7a-f4cffcb08c4e","ttft_stream_ms":1661,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":1661,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
